implementationPlan.description:
Docs + test: `### moe.create_task` and one createTask.test.ts case (DoD 1-4). Same docs rules as step 1.

(a) docs/MCP_SERVER.md, create_task. Source: createTask.ts:38 (schema enum of six), :76-78 (any other truthy status is INVALID_INPUT `Invalid status: must be one of: ...`, before any write), :174 and state/taskStore.ts:334 (an omitted status is BACKLOG).
- Parameters: replace `  status?: string,` (unique; anchor it together with the `  taskRails?: string[],` line above it) with
  `  status?: "BACKLOG" | "PLANNING" | "AWAITING_APPROVAL" | "WORKING" | "REVIEW" | "DONE",  // omitted = BACKLOG; BLOCKED and ARCHIVED are refused`
  The comment must contain the exact text `omitted = BACKLOG` (checkRef 1).
- Input refusals: replace the bullet `- an unknown \`status\` or \`priority\`;` with one that states the rule and contains the backticked token `BLOCKED` (checkRef 1). Suggested:
  `- a \`status\` outside the six listed above (a task cannot be created \`BLOCKED\` or \`ARCHIVED\`), or an unknown \`priority\`;`
  The sentence after the list already says each refusal is `INVALID_INPUT` naming the field; keep it.

(b) packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/createTask.test.ts. Add `import fs from 'fs';` and `import path from 'path';` at the top (as createTask.shape.test.ts does), and ONE `it` at the end of the first describe (`moe.create_task`, whose beforeEach loads epic-1 and no tasks). Capture the refusal the way createTask.shape.test.ts expectRefused does. Suggested:
  it('refuses a status it cannot create and writes no task; an omitted status gives BACKLOG', async () => {
    const tool = createTaskTool(h.state);
    for (const status of ['BLOCKED', 'ARCHIVED']) {
      const err = await tool.handler({ epicId: 'epic-1', title: `parked ${status}`, status }, h.state).then(
        () => null,
        (e: unknown) => e as { codeName?: string; message: string },
      );
      expect(err?.codeName).toBe('INVALID_INPUT');
      expect(err?.message).toContain('Invalid status');
    }
    expect(h.state.tasks.size).toBe(0);
    expect(fs.readdirSync(path.join(h.moePath, 'tasks'))).toEqual([]);

    const result = await tool.handler({ epicId: 'epic-1', title: 'No status given' }, h.state) as { task: Task };
    expect(result.task.status).toBe('BACKLOG');
    expect(h.state.getTask(result.task.id)?.status).toBe('BACKLOG');
  });
Planning dry run in a snapshot of 80078651: the case passes. It fails with the :76-78 check removed (`expected undefined to be 'INVALID_INPUT'`: that check is the only guard, so a BLOCKED row would be written), and with taskStore's default changed to PLANNING (`expected 'PLANNING' to be 'BACKLOG'`). Error handling: the test asserts the refusal's codeName and that no row reaches memory or disk, so a write-then-throw regression fails it too.

Docs + test: `### moe.create_team`, `### moe.get_pending_questions` and one getPendingQuestions.test.ts case (DoD 1-4). Same docs rules as step 1.

(a) create_team. Source: createTeam.ts:7 (VALID_ROLES includes governor), :17 (schema), :40-41 (INVALID_INPUT for any other role), the idempotency lookup after validateTeamName: getTeamByNameAndRole(name, role) in state/teamStore.ts:32-37 matches name AND role (null === null). Also claimNextTask.ts:482-493 (a seat that resolves to governor gets hasNext:false and a moe.enter_governance nextAction) and util/workerRole.ts resolveWorkerRole (team role first).
- role line: `  role?: 'architect' | 'worker' | 'qa' | 'governor', // Optional: team role (omit for project team)`.
- Intro: its second sentence ('If `role` is omitted, idempotency is name-only and the team is project-wide.') is wrong, and createTeam.test.ts (t2) pins the opposite: a role-less 'Gov' create next to a 'Gov' governor team makes a second team. Suggested replacement of the whole intro:
  Create a team or return an existing team with the same name and role (idempotent; the name is trimmed first). If `role` is omitted, the team is project-wide, and only a role-less team of that name is returned: a role-less create never adopts a role-bound team that shares its name.
- After the Returns block, ONE paragraph with the exact lead-in `**Governor teams:**` and `enter_governance` on that line. Suggested:
  **Governor teams:** `role: 'governor'` creates a governor team. Its members act as governors, because a seat's team role wins over its id prefix (`util/workerRole.ts`), so `moe.claim_next_task` answers them `hasNext: false` with a `moe.enter_governance` nextAction instead of a claim.

(b) get_pending_questions. Source: getPendingQuestions.ts:45-48 (includeArchived, default false), :119-123 (archiving does not clear hasPendingQuestion; ARCHIVED is skipped unless includeArchived === true).
- Parameters: after the epicId line add `  includeArchived?: boolean,   // default: false — ARCHIVED tasks are left out unless true`.
- Notes: after the maxContentChars bullet add one bullet containing `includeArchived: true` (checkRef 1). Suggested:
  - `ARCHIVED` tasks are left out by default, because archiving does not clear `hasPendingQuestion`; pass `includeArchived: true` to include them.

(c) packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/getPendingQuestions.test.ts: ONE `it` at the end of the describe. It needs two tasks, each with hasPendingQuestion and one unanswered human comment with a fixed timestamp: task-live (harness default BACKLOG, order 1) and task-shelved (status 'ARCHIVED', order 2). Suggested:
  it('leaves an ARCHIVED task out by default and returns it with includeArchived: true', async () => {
    h.setupMoeFolder();
    h.createEpic();
    const question = (id: string) => [{ id, author: 'human', content: `Still open? ${id}`, timestamp: '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z' }];
    h.createTask({ id: 'task-live', order: 1, hasPendingQuestion: true, comments: question('c-live') });
    h.createTask({ id: 'task-shelved', order: 2, status: 'ARCHIVED', hasPendingQuestion: true, comments: question('c-shelved') });
    await h.state.load();

    type Res = { totalMatches: number; tasks: Array<{ taskId: string; questions: Array<{ commentId: string }> }> };
    const tool = getPendingQuestionsTool(h.state);
    const byDefault = await tool.handler({}, h.state) as Res;
    expect(byDefault.tasks.map((t) => t.taskId)).toEqual(['task-live']);
    expect(byDefault.totalMatches).toBe(1);

    const withArchived = await tool.handler({ includeArchived: true }, h.state) as Res;
    expect(withArchived.tasks.map((t) => t.taskId)).toEqual(['task-live', 'task-shelved']);
    expect(withArchived.tasks[1].questions.map((q) => q.commentId)).toEqual(['c-shelved']);
  });
Planning dry run: the case passes at 80078651. It fails when :123 is deleted (the default then returns both rows) and when it skips ARCHIVED unconditionally (includeArchived: true then returns only task-live). The live control row stops the default assertion passing on an empty result. Error handling: the case asserts exact row sets, not truthiness, so a filter that drops everything fails too.
